---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const domainColor = '#3b82f6'; // Blue for Intake
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Intake & Triage Agent — Medivora"
  description="Architecture and capabilities of the Medivora Intake & Triage Agent for automating ICSR processing from unstructured sources."
>
  <article class="agent-detail-page">
    
    <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <header class="agent-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/agents">← Back to Agents</a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span class="domain-tag" style={`--dc: ${domainColor}`}>Pharmacovigilance</span>
          <span class="phase-tag">Phase 1 · Intake</span>
          <span class="date-tag">Last reviewed: Jun 2025</span>
        </div>
        
        <h1 class="agent-title">Intake &amp; Triage Agent</h1>
        <p class="agent-tagline">Automated ingestion, translation, and structured data extraction of ICSRs.</p>

        <div class="agent-hero-pattern" style="--agent-accent: rgba(59,130,246,0.12)"></div>
        
        <div class="reading-meta">
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📖 12 min read</span>
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📅 Updated 2025-06-02</span>
          <button class="btn-print" onclick="window.print()">🖨 Save as PDF</button>
        </div>

        <nav class="pipeline-indicator" aria-label="ICSR Pipeline Position">
          <a href="/agents/intake-triage" class="pipeline-step active">Intake</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/meddra-coding" class="pipeline-step">Coding</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/medical-review" class="pipeline-step">Review</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/aggregate-reporting" class="pipeline-step">Reporting</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/literature-monitoring" class="pipeline-step">Literature</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/regulatory-intelligence" class="pipeline-step">RegIntel</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="agent-metrics">
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">70%+<sup>[1]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Reduction in manual data entry</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">99%<sup>[2]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Extraction recall on unstructured text</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">&lt;2 mins<sup>[3]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Average processing time per case</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
          <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.4); margin-bottom:0.6rem;">References & Sources</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[1] McKinsey & Company, 'AI in Drug Safety Operations', 2024 <span class="risk-med" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Projected)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[2] FDA Technology Modernization Action Plan (TMAP), 2023 <span class="" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Theoretical)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[3] Internal benchmark, GPT-4o structured extraction pipeline <span class="risk-low" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Measured)</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="reviewed-by-band">
          <div class="rb-icon">✓</div>
          <div class="rb-text">
            Content reviewed by <strong>Kritnandan</strong>, B.Tech BSBE (IIT Kanpur) | Last review: Jun 2025 | Review cadence: Quarterly
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ── THE PROBLEM ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light problem-section">
      <div class="wrap content-grid">
        <div class="cg-main">
          <h2>The Triage Bottleneck</h2>
          <p class="lead-text">
            Safety departments are overwhelmed by the sheer volume of adverse event reports arriving via emails, literature, portals, and patient support programs. Data entry teams manually transcribe unstructured narratives into safety databases, leading to backlogs and transcription errors.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Medivora Intake &amp; Triage Agent eliminates this bottleneck. It reads emails, OCRs PDFs, translates foreign languages, and extracts patient demographics, reporter details, suspect drugs, and adverse events into a structured E2B (R3) format ready for medical review.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="cg-side info-panel">
          <h4>Agent Profile</h4>
          <dl class="agent-specs">
            <dt>Data Inputs</dt>
            <dd>Emails, PDF forms (CIOMS, MedWatch), scientific literature, social media.</dd>
            <dt>Core AI Models</dt>
            <dd>Vision-Language Models for OCR, LLMs with structured JSON output capabilities.</dd>
            <dt>Key Outputs</dt>
            <dd>E2B (R3) XML files, prepopulated Argus/Veeva Vault Safety draft cases.</dd>
            <dt>Standards</dt>
            <dd>ICH E2B (R3), GVP Module VI.</dd>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── ARCHITECTURE ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark arch-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Agent Architecture &amp; Workflow</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          A ReAct loop orchestrates the intake process, extracting entities via structured prompt engineering and validating them against E2B standards before committing to the safety database.
        </p>
        
        <div class="diagram-container">
          <pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    classDef external fill:#1a1a1a,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px,color:#888
    classDef input fill:#112a22,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef agent fill:#0a192f,stroke:#64ffda,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef db fill:#2d1b2e,stroke:#e05c8a,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef hitl fill:#3a2a00,stroke:#e8a838,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef output fill:#112a22,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff

    subgraph "Intake Sources"
        direction TB
        Email["Email Inbox"]:::external
        Lit["Scientific Literature"]:::external
        Forms["PDF Forms"]:::external
    end

    subgraph "Processing Layer"
        direction TB
        OCR["Vision/OCR Agent"]:::input
        Translate["Translation Agent"]:::agent
    end

    subgraph "Reasoning Layer"
        direction TB
        Triage(["Triage & Extraction Agent<br>(Structured LLM)"]):::agent
        ValidDB[("Validation Rules<br>(E2B schema)")]:::db
    end

    subgraph "Action Layer"
        direction TB
        HITL(["Data Entry QC<br>(Human Review)"]):::hitl
        SafetyDB["Argus / Vault Safety"]:::output
    end

    Email --> OCR
    Lit --> Translate
    Forms --> OCR

    OCR --> Triage
    Translate --> Triage

    Triage -- "Extracts JSON" --> ValidDB
    ValidDB -- "Validated Entities" --> HITL

    HITL -- "Approves" --> SafetyDB

    linkStyle default stroke:#444,stroke-width:2px;
          </pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CORE CAPABILITIES ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light caps-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-title-dark">Core Capabilities</h2>
        <div class="caps-grid">
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">1</div>
            <h3>Multimodal Ingestion</h3>
            <p>Handles scanned faxes, handwritten MedWatch forms, and complex email chains using state-of-the-art Vision-Language Models.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">2</div>
            <h3>Structured E2B Extraction</h3>
            <p>Extracts data strictly according to E2B (R3) schemas. Converts free-text ages (e.g., "a toddler") into structured age groups, and identifies suspect vs. concomitant medications.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">3</div>
            <h3>Validity Assessment</h3>
            <p>Automatically checks if a report constitutes a valid ICSR by verifying the four minimum criteria: identifiable patient, identifiable reporter, suspect drug, and adverse event.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">4</div>
            <h3>Duplicate Detection</h3>
            <p>Uses fuzzy matching against the safety database to detect follow-up information and prevent the creation of duplicate cases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── UNDER THE HOOD ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark under-hood-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Under the Hood</span>
        <h2>Architectural Deep Dive</h2>
        
        <div class="uh-grid">
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>System Prompt Formulation</h3>
            <p>The Intake Agent is bound by strict extraction rules to prevent hallucination of clinical facts. It operates with a temperature of 0.0 to ensure deterministic output.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">system_prompt.txt</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code>You are an expert Pharmacovigilance Intake Agent.
Your objective is to extract ICSR entities from the provided text.

CRITICAL RULES:
1. ONLY extract information explicitly stated in the text. 
   Do NOT infer or guess medical history.
2. If an element (e.g., patient age) is missing, output null.
3. Map all dates to ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).
4. Identify if the four minimum criteria for a valid ICSR are met:
   - Identifiable patient
   - Identifiable reporter
   - Suspect drug
   - Adverse event

Output the result using the extract_icsr_entities tool.</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>Tool Calling Schema (E2B Mapping)</h3>
            <p>The agent commits data to the safety database via a structured JSON schema that maps directly to ICH E2B (R3) data elements.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">schema.json</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code>{
  "name": "extract_icsr_entities",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "is_valid_icsr": { "type": "boolean" },
      "patient": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "age": { "type": "number", "description": "E2B: D.2.2a" },
          "sex": { "type": "string", "enum": ["M", "F", "U"] }
        }
      },
      "events": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "drugs": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": { 
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
             "name": { "type": "string" },
             "role": { "type": "string", "enum": ["suspect", "concomitant"] }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guardrails-box">
          <h3>Guardrails & Failure Modes</h3>
          <ul class="guardrail-list">
            <li><strong>OCR Degradation:</strong> Handwritten forms or highly degraded faxes often cause vision-model hallucinations. Confidence scores below 85% automatically route the case to a human queue.</li>
            <li><strong>Contradictory Timelines:</strong> If a narrative states a patient started a drug in 2023 but the event occurred in 2022, the agent is instructed to flag an anomaly rather than attempt to resolve the logical paradox.</li>
            <li><strong>Human-in-the-Loop (HITL):</strong> The agent <em>never</em> commits a case directly to regulatory authorities. It creates a "Draft" case in the safety database (e.g., Argus) for medical review.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── SAMPLE DEMO ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark" id="sample-demo">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Interactive Demo</span>
        <h2>See It in Action</h2>
        <h3>Sample Case Walkthrough</h3>
        <span class="synthetic-watermark">Synthetic Data — Illustrative Only</span>
        <div class="sample-demo">
          <div class="demo-panel">
            <div class="demo-panel-header">Input</div>
            <div class="demo-panel-body"><pre is:raw style="white-space:pre-wrap; margin:0; font-size:0.8rem; color:#a8b2d1;">From: dr.smith@hospital.org\nSubject: Adverse event report\n\nDear Safety Team,\n\nI am writing to report that my patient, a 67-year-old female, developed severe hepatotoxicity approximately 14 days after initiating treatment with Drug-X 200mg daily for rheumatoid arthritis. ALT was elevated to 5x ULN. The drug was discontinued and the patient is recovering.\n\nDr. Smith, Consultant Rheumatologist</pre></div>
          </div>
          <div class="demo-panel">
            <div class="demo-panel-header">Agent Output</div>
            <div class="demo-panel-body"><pre is:raw style="white-space:pre-wrap; margin:0; font-size:0.8rem; color:#a8b2d1;">{\n  "is_valid_icsr": true,\n  "patient": {\n    "age": 67,\n    "age_unit": "Year",\n    "sex": "F"\n  },\n  "reporter": {\n    "name": "Dr. Smith",\n    "qualification": "Physician"\n  },\n  "drugs": [{\n    "name": "Drug-X",\n    "dose": "200mg",\n    "route": "Oral",\n    "role": "suspect"\n  }],\n  "events": [{\n    "verbatim": "severe hepatotoxicity",\n    "onset_days": 14\n  }],\n  "action_taken": "Drug withdrawn",\n  "outcome": "Recovering"\n}</pre></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── RISK & COMPLIANCE ────────────────────────────────── -->
